From: Paul Spooren <mail@aparcar.org>
Subject: dlink-sge-image: initialize the signature length

EVP_PKEY_sign() takes the size of the signature buffer in *siglen and
fails if it is too small. siglen is not initialized, so the result
depends on whatever the stack holds: with some builds both signatures
are written, with others signing fails and the image carries 1024 zero
bytes instead. The same firmware thus differs between build hosts.

Set siglen to the size of the buffer before each call. The signatures
are deterministic PKCS#1 v1.5 signatures, so they match the ones of
images built where signing happened to work.

Signed-off-by: Paul Spooren <mail@aparcar.org>
---
 src/dlink-sge-image.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/src/dlink-sge-image.c
+++ b/src/dlink-sge-image.c
@@ -179,6 +179,7 @@ void image_encrypt(void)
 	fwrite(&sigret[0], 1, RSA_KEY_LENGTH_BYTES, output_file);
 
 	// sign md_before
+	siglen = sizeof(sigret);
 	EVP_PKEY_sign(rsa_ctx, &sigret[0], &siglen, &md_before[0], SHA512_DIGEST_LENGTH);
 	printf("\nsigned before:\n");
 	for (i = 0; i < RSA_KEY_LENGTH_BYTES; i++)
@@ -186,6 +187,7 @@ void image_encrypt(void)
 	fwrite(&sigret[0], 1, RSA_KEY_LENGTH_BYTES, output_file);
 
 	// sign md_post
+	siglen = sizeof(sigret);
 	EVP_PKEY_sign(rsa_ctx, &sigret[0], &siglen, &md_post[0], SHA512_DIGEST_LENGTH);
 	printf("\nsigned post:\n");
 	for (i = 0; i < RSA_KEY_LENGTH_BYTES; i++)
